# A1 joins "conduct being either good or bad" to "acts are really good and bad". Both take "good/bad" as an act's real moral quality, so A1 is not a bridge.
# "real" in "really good and bad" and in "real, genuine possibilities" belongs to two different claims, so it is not one claim used in two senses.
